        42.71014404296875,
        351.3055725097656,
        438.229248046875,
        360.5408935546875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "and stratiﬁed resampling procedures. The condition in equation (24) is not usually satisﬁed",
      "bbox": [
        42.71014404296875,
        363.26068115234375,
        438.22723388671875,
        372.4960021972656
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "as in practice, for computational efﬁciency, On is usually drawn ﬁrst according to a proba-",
      "bbox": [
        42.71014404296875,
        375.2157897949219,
        438.2273864746094,
        385.9457092285156
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "bility distribution s.·|Wn/ such that equation (23) holds (i.e. without explicit reference to An)",
      "bbox": [
        42.71031188964844,
        386.33428955078125,
        438.23175048828125,
        396.4065856933594
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "and the offspring then matched to their parents. More precisely, once On has been sampled,",
      "bbox": [
        42.711578369140625,
        399.1263732910156,
        438.23095703125,
        409.8561096191406
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "this is followed by a deterministic allocation procedure of the offspring particles to the",
      "bbox": [
        42.71075439453125,
        411.0815734863281,
        438.23193359375,
        420.31689453125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "parents, which deﬁnes indices; for example the O1",
      "bbox": [
        42.71075439453125,
        421.13232421875,
        268.33978271484375,
        432.2720031738281
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
